  "answer": "Double circulation is a process in which blood passes through the heart twice during one complete cycle. In humans, this is important because it ensures that oxygenated blood is efficiently delivered to all parts of the body while deoxygenated blood is returned to the lungs for re-oxygenation. The double circulation consists of two parts: pulmonary circulation and systemic circulation. Pulmonary circulation involves the movement of blood from the right ventricle to the lungs and back to the left atrium, while systemic circulation involves the movement of blood from the left ventricle to the rest of the body and back to the right atrium. This system allows for efficient gas exchange and nutrient distribution throughout the body.",
